The sidekick prompt endpoint sets status 204 but still sets Content-Type: application/json and returns a streamed response with no body. 204 responses should not include a body (and typically omit Content-Type). Consider returning a normal empty 204 response without streaming, or switch to 202/200 if you intend a streamed/JSON response.
```suggestion
        const parentID = c.req.valid("param").sessionID
        const body = c.req.valid("json")
        // Resolve the sidekick session ID before firing the async prompt
        // so errors are attributed to the sidekick, not the parent
        const sidekick = await Sidekick.ensure(parentID)
        Sidekick.prompt({ parentID, text: body.text, model: body.model }).catch((err) => {
          log.error("sidekick prompt failed", { sessionID: sidekick.id, error: err })
          Bus.publish(Session.Event.Error, {
            sessionID: sidekick.id,
            error: new NamedError.Unknown({ message: err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err) }).toObject(),
          })
        })
        c.status(204)
        return c.body(null)
```

`refresh()` can return without updating `ModelsDev.Data` when another process wins the `Flock` and updates the cache file: the inner `if (fresh()) return` exits the locked section with `undefined`, and the outer code only calls `ModelsDev.Data.reset()` on `result.ok`. If this process had already evaluated `Data()` (e.g. it fell back to the bundled snapshot while waiting for the other process to fetch/write `models.json`), it will keep serving stale in-memory data until restart. Consider resetting `ModelsDev.Data` when the lock is acquired but no fetch occurs because the file became fresh while waiting (e.g. detect that case and call `ModelsDev.Data.reset()` so subsequent reads pick up the new file).
```suggestion
      if (fresh()) return { refreshed: true as const }
      const fetched = await fetchApi()
      return { refreshed: false as const, ...fetched }
    }).catch((e) => {
      log.error("Failed to fetch models.dev", {
        error: e,
